    "DEBIAN-CVE-2019-1010022": {
      "condition": "aarch64_guard",
      "ecosystem": "Debian:13",
      "source": "glibc",
      "source_version": "2.41-12+deb13u5",
      "advisory_sha256": "a76450a4a96c9ff8668f7b7d3bc5cfca5cdc02d7430b6b7cfc3fb3427454415c",
      "cna_sha256": "d93155969ac931b1d31e3996ef43956860bfea9409157ee1f301c80390358824",
      "reason": "Upstream bug 22850 describes x86/x86-64 stack_guard in the thread control block. Every native object is AArch64. The actual loader exports a read-only global __stack_chk_guard outside a newly created thread stack, with the same reference in that thread. This is a verified platform precondition difference, not a conclusion based solely on disputed status.",
      "references": [
        "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2019-1010022"
      ]
    },
    "DEBIAN-CVE-2019-1010023": {
      "condition": "trusted_native_inputs",
      "ecosystem": "Debian:13",
      "source": "glibc",
      "source_version": "2.41-12+deb13u5",
      "advisory_sha256": "ae9e7f4911133734b450688792cdcbd6ebe7d0fb6ad3d52eed1eb451ae2efa7c",
      "cna_sha256": "f31f3d48c55e9280702a0c5712930e549e015a79eee725e9692d9cd71823bbf9",
      "reason": "Every ELF loadable-segment table in the immutable images is inspected without executing inspected files and has ordered load segments. The exact qualified application loads only reviewed frozen/native objects from read-only image paths; owned server/worker sources expose no process/native-call/dynamic-code entry point. Qualification checks read-only roots and fixed code mounts. No untrusted ELF inspection/loading interface is admitted. Running ldd or native plugins on untrusted files is outside this reviewed profile.",
      "references": [
        "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2019-1010023"
      ]
    },
    "DEBIAN-CVE-2026-84243": {
      "condition": "fixed_locale",
      "ecosystem": "Debian:13",
      "source": "glibc",
      "source_version": "2.41-12+deb13u5",
      "advisory_sha256": "e5c0daa277fa2f06d773b2accf52bf3a556d096f2767384aacc36b0c94535122",
      "cna_sha256": "31d4067d2b0ea256acc500d6ff5f2883fd800e7281d5695034b252fb313a8da7",
      "reason": "The actual native process selects C.UTF-8, with fixed LANG=LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 and LANGUAGE=C in images and qualified running roles. The upstream advisory states LANGUAGE is ignored for C/C.<encoding>/POSIX LC_MESSAGES. No external locale/environment selection interface is present in the exact owned source. This recorded precondition is rechecked and does not approve other locale configurations.",
      "references": [
        "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-84243"
      ]
    },
    "DEBIAN-CVE-2005-2541": {
      "condition": "unprivileged_archive_path",
      "ecosystem": "Debian:13",
      "source": "tar",
      "source_version": "1.35+dfsg-3.1",
      "advisory_sha256": "497c3b768c9aa1560f5136ed38ff6b03fc98e66c89984f573eaad374e3b352f0",
      "cna_sha256": "b333988692f6ef9fb83bf4ab754f0133686c9e424620c874666c17682ccb7ed5",
      "reason": "The qualified runtime is non-root, read-only, zero-capability and no-new-privileges. Native probes verify the actual non-root user and kernel flag. The cold-copy helper parses bounded physical USTAR itself and rejects setuid/setgid bits, links and special files before writing; it does not invoke tar for extraction. Owned application sources expose no process-execution/archive CLI interface. The tar warning/privilege-preservation case is outside this exact execution path; package behavior itself is not claimed fixed.",
      "references": [
        "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2005-2541"
      ]
    },
    "DEBIAN-CVE-2026-84785": {
      "condition": "no_incoming_quic",
      "ecosystem": "Debian:13",
      "source": "openssl",
      "source_version": "3.5.9-1~deb13u1+ezllmrouter1",
      "advisory_sha256": "f6d0880c31c7da7d496dda76f2c1371046ceee922765dfdbe454c9e994e01fee",
      "cna_sha256": "c56281ae4e0683734a56fb867fa145d7fc317de7d40cf88f810a00fbea08e2f6",
      "reason": "The qualified Python/Node roles use TCP HTTP/TLS and expose no incoming QUIC stream interface. Full application ELF closure has no QUIC method, stream-acceptance or incoming-policy API caller. The owned sources expose no native-call or dynamic-code interface. The canonical advisory requires non-default acceptance of peer-initiated QUIC streams; this precondition is false in the exact reviewed profile. This is not an upstream code-fix claim.",
      "references": [
        "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-84785"
      ]
    }
  },
  "scope": "Exact disposable-qualified Linux ARM64 profile only. These not_affected preconditions do not fix upstream packages or approve other profiles, arbitrary native execution or production acceptance.",
  "native_advisory_updates": {
    "DEBIAN-CVE-2026-107494": {
      "native_build": "f39d002d3595dc6020735be2e4123b1c6ac3ada2812f508db92699ce1b4420d0",
      "patch_sha256": "c1726a50d589b2dc289727865c184382c2bd846733ddb139427062713ebeb5bd",
      "previous_advisory": {
        "id": "DEBIAN-CVE-2026-107494",
        "details": "Issue summary: The QUIC stack queues a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame also for retransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames. This allows a remote malicious QUIC stack to queue an unlimited number of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames.  Impact summary: A malicious remote QUIC peer can trigger an out-of-memory condition causing a Denial of Service.  CWE: CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling  Description: The earlier fix for CVE-2026-84784 was not complete. It failed to ignore retransmissions of the NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame. The QUIC implementation created and inserted a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame for every retransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame it received and there was no limit on how many RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames were queued. This allows a malicious remote QUIC stack to trigger an out-of-memory (OOM) condition.  FIPS impact: no The FIPS module is not affected as the QUIC implementation is outside the OpenSSL FIPS module boundary.",
        "modified": "2026-11-23T14:00:05.423724768Z",
